<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Three-stage tree diagrams with equal probabilities</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(ix=1)"]]Wanjiku guesses the answers to three multiple-choice questions. Each question has four options, so each guess is right with probability \(\dfrac{1}{4}\), independently.[[elif test="is(ix=2)"]]Baraka guesses the answers to three questions, each with three options. Each guess is right with probability \(\dfrac{1}{3}\), independently.[[elif test="is(ix=3)"]]A farmer plants three bean seeds of a new variety. Each seed germinates with probability \(\dfrac{3}{4}\), independently.[[elif test="is(ix=4)"]]On a July day in Nyeri the probability of a sunny day is \(\dfrac{3}{10}\). Assume the weather on three July days is independent.[[elif test="is(ix=5)"]]Nafula's matatu passes three traffic lights. Each light is green when the matatu reaches it with probability \(\dfrac{3}{5}\), independently.[[elif test="is(ix=6)"]]A farmer in Bungoma plants three maize seeds. Each seed germinates with probability \(\dfrac{7}{10}\), independently.[[elif test="is(ix=7)"]]Muthoni transplants three sukuma wiki seedlings. Each survives transplanting with probability \(\dfrac{4}{5}\), independently.[[elif test="is(ix=8)"]]On a tea farm in Kericho, each tea bush survives the dry season with probability \(\dfrac{9}{10}\), independently. Three bushes are chosen.[[elif test="is(ix=9)"]]At a large school, the probability that a learner chosen at random walks to school is \(\dfrac{2}{5}\). Three learners are chosen at random, independently.[[elif test="is(ix=10)"]]A spinner has four equal sectors, one of them red. It is spun three times. Each spin lands on red with probability \(\dfrac{1}{4}\), independently.[[/if]]</p><p>A tree diagram with three stages may help. Write S when the event happens and F when it does not.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find the probability that [[if test="is(ix=1)"]]all three guesses are right[[elif test="is(ix=2)"]]all three guesses are right[[elif test="is(ix=3)"]]all three seeds germinate[[elif test="is(ix=4)"]]all three days are sunny[[elif test="is(ix=5)"]]all three lights are green[[elif test="is(ix=6)"]]all three seeds germinate[[elif test="is(ix=7)"]]all three seedlings survive[[elif test="is(ix=8)"]]all three bushes survive[[elif test="is(ix=9)"]]all three walk to school[[elif test="is(ix=10)"]]all three spins land on red[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the probability that [[if test="is(ix=1)"]]exactly two guesses are right[[elif test="is(ix=2)"]]exactly two guesses are right[[elif test="is(ix=3)"]]exactly two seeds germinate[[elif test="is(ix=4)"]]exactly two days are sunny[[elif test="is(ix=5)"]]exactly two lights are green[[elif test="is(ix=6)"]]exactly two seeds germinate[[elif test="is(ix=7)"]]exactly two seedlings survive[[elif test="is(ix=8)"]]exactly two bushes survive[[elif test="is(ix=9)"]]exactly two walk to school[[elif test="is(ix=10)"]]exactly two spins land on red[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the probability that [[if test="is(ix=1)"]]at least one guess is right[[elif test="is(ix=2)"]]at least one guess is right[[elif test="is(ix=3)"]]at least one seed germinates[[elif test="is(ix=4)"]]at least one day is sunny[[elif test="is(ix=5)"]]at least one light is green[[elif test="is(ix=6)"]]at least one seed germinates[[elif test="is(ix=7)"]]at least one seedling survives[[elif test="is(ix=8)"]]at least one bush survives[[elif test="is(ix=9)"]]at least one walks to school[[elif test="is(ix=10)"]]at least one spin lands on red[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Each stage has two branches: S with probability \({@p@}\) and F with probability \({@1-p@}\). The tree has eight paths; multiply along a path and add the paths you need.</p><p>(a) One path, SSS: \({@p@} \times {@p@} \times {@p@} = {@ta1@}\).</p><p>(b) Three paths have exactly two S: SSF, SFS and FSS. Each has probability \({@p@} \times {@p@} \times {@1-p@} = {@p^2*(1-p)@}\), so the answer is \(3 \times {@p^2*(1-p)@} = {@ta2@}\).</p><p>(c) <q>At least one</q> is everything except FFF: \(1 - ({@1-p@})^3 = 1 - {@(1-p)^3@} = {@ta3@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
